{"timestamp":"2026-09-04T10:53:27.255Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_08df5c6668f07f38016a9aa321dfb887d29bb59d8e2fb8e1c9","status":"completed","call_id":"call_qrqjpzBBz4NIHEw0s1ML6gLm","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /var/lib/containerd/io.containerd.snapshotter.v1.overlayfs/snapshots/3/fs/root/projects/tiered-serve/tiered_serve/dual_memory_loader/timing.py\\n@@\\n-            # ── Separate Compute from WEIGHT Decomp ──\\n-            # The decode GEMM blocks on cur_stream until its WEIGHT\\n-            # decompression (on decomp_weight_stream) completes — the weight IS\\n-            # the GEMM operand, so the GEMM cannot start until decomp lands.\\n-            # Only ~6ms of that block surfaces as the in-graph _v1_wwait; the\\n-            # rest stays inside the exec window, which is why Compute(LLM) read\\n-            # ~= WDecomp ~= GPUFwd even though the real GEMM is tiny.  Carve the\\n-            # weight-decomp union out so Compute is GEMM+attention only.\\n-            #\\n-            # KV decode must NOT be carved (it used to be — that was a bug).\\n-            # It is prefetched one layer ahead (start_kv_decompress(L+1) in\\n-            # _before_replay(L), finish in _after_replay(L)) and runs on\\n-            # batch_decomp_stream CONCURRENTLY with the productive GEMM of the\\n-            # next graph piece — it does not block that GEMM.  Attention's real\\n-            # wait for its OWN layer's KV is the exec_attn_barrier, and that\\n-            # wait is ALREADY removed above via _v1_kv_wait (wait_intervals).\\n-            # Subtracting the decode interval a second time here removed real,\\n-            # concurrent GEMM from Compute, so Compute SHRANK when --kv-comp was\\n-            # enabled (C.A.O b128 165.6 → C.A.O+KVComp 139.0, exactly the ~22ms\\n-            # decode carved out) even though the real compute is unchanged.\\n-            # Leave KV decode in Compute and report it separately as KVDecomp,\\n-            # a concurrent stream-busy metric that overlaps Compute by design\\n-            # (so Compute + KVDecomp may exceed GPUFwd — that overlap is the\\n-            # decode being hidden under compute).  Stall is unaffected:\\n-            # compute_union below unions the decomp intervals back in anyway.\\n+            # ── Productive Compute vs graph-piece residual ──\\n+            # Keep the historical subtraction only as ExecResidual.  It cannot\\n+            # establish productive-kernel time because an unobserved transitive\\n+            # weight dependency remains inside the graph-piece envelope.  The\\n+            # authoritative Compute source is the complete set of projection /\\n+            # attention markers assembled near the top of calc_times.\\n             if wdecomp_union:\\n-                llm_active_intervals = self._subtract_intervals(\\n-                    llm_active_intervals, wdecomp_union)\\n-            llm_brk = sum(e - b for b, e in llm_active_intervals)\\n+                exec_residual_intervals = self._subtract_intervals(\\n+                    exec_residual_intervals, wdecomp_union)\\n+            exec_residual_brk = sum(\\n+                e - b for b, e in exec_residual_intervals)\\n+            llm_active_intervals = productive_compute_intervals\\n+            llm_brk = (sum(e - b for b, e in llm_active_intervals)\\n+                       if compute_markers_valid else None)\\n+            dense_compute_brk = (\\n+                sum(e - b for b, e in dense_compute_intervals)\\n+                if compute_markers_valid else None)\\n+            fused_weight_compute_brk = (\\n+                sum(e - b for b, e in fused_weight_compute_intervals)\\n+                if compute_markers_valid else None)\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a06c08-dab1-7df3-80fd-f5a977ff60b7","create_time"